On Dec 4, 9:02 pm, Cuboidz <Dieter.Be...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I'm pretty new to Nethack, and I've come to dislike shops because of
> all the drudgery involved in putting them to good use: price-ID'ing
> scrolls, stealing stuff with your pet ...
>
> So I'm wondering whether it is feasible to just use shops for shopping
> only? And in the same vein: what do you (usually) do when you
> encounter a shop?

I price-ID scrolls until I have identify, enchant armor/remove curse,
and enchant weapon.  I'll price-ID lamps too (for magic).

Otherwise I just buy what I need, unless I've lucked into a magic
whistle or something and there's something that's really worth the
effort.  Early on I may spend a bit more effort if it'll get me magic
resistance or something like that, but usually it's easier just to get
the money and buy it.


